) to require minlen=12 and minclass=3 via a drop-in file, verified enforcement with pwscore, and completed the mandatory single-node restart/recovery evidence protocol.\",\"actions_performed\":[\"Inspected existing libpwquality install and empty pwquality.conf.d/ drop-in directory\",\"Created /etc/security/pwquality.conf.d/10-complexity.conf with minlen=12 and minclass=3\",\"Confirmed pam_pwquality.so is wired into /etc/pam.d/system-auth and /etc/pam.d/password-auth\",\"Created a throwaway test user and used pwscore to confirm a <12-char password fails, a 12+ char 2-class password fails minclass, and a 12+ char 3-class random password passes\",\"Deleted the test user\",\"Captured pre-restart boot_id and re-verified config/PAM state\",\"Issued a backgrounded systemctl reboot on node1 so the ack returned before disconnection\",\"Polled node1 until exec succeeded again, confirming a new boot_id\",\"Re-verified post-reboot: config file present, PAM wiring present, weak password rejected, valid 12-char/3-class password accepted\"],\"evidence\":[{\"requirement\":\"New user passwords require minlen=12 and at least 3 character classes\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-b7d4d06a1f9447a6\",\"cmd-d5c99ff4dc2242b7\",\"cmd-ae353c21095a47cf\",\"cmd-a0911c8c3a2f4ccf\",\"cmd-a1f75b29efbf458e\"],\"summary\":\"Created pwquality drop-in with minlen=12/minclass=3, confirmed PAM wiring, and verified via pwscore that a short password fails minlen, a 12+ char 2-class password fails minclass, and a 12+ char 3-class random password is accepted (score 36).\"},{\"requirement\":\"Pre-restart healthy baseline on node1\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-0ec998a595e04182\"],\"summary\":\"Captured boot_id d052eb57-c81d-4309-ae7f-bce362073ff9 and confirmed the pwquality config file and PAM hook were present before restart.\"},{\"requirement\":\"node1 restart acknowledgement returned before disconnection\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-75433305dfc84250\"],\"summary\":\"Backgrounded systemctl reboot command returned 'rebooting' immediately, before the node dropped.\"},{\"requirement\":\"node1 boot identity changed after restart\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-c9910acbcb414385\",\"cmd-e9ccfdc965fa46b6\",\"cmd-55ff181aeb8f4c30\",\"cmd-1995280cbe5146cf\"],\"summary\":\"boot_id was unchanged then connection dropped (node rebooting), then exec succeeded again with a new boot_id 7a149124-e592-42b1-b245-7c02ab02aac7, proving an actual reboot occurred.\"},{\"requirement\":\"node1 post-restart recovery of required config/service state\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-725727ad45fc460b\"],\"summary\":\"After reboot, confirmed new uptime, pwquality.conf.d file intact, PAM hooks intact, and functional re-verification (short password rejected, valid 3-class 12-char password accepted).\"}]}","structured_output":{"status":"completed","summary":"Configured pam_pwquality on node1 (CentOS Stream 10) to require minlen=12 and minclass=3 via a drop-in file, verified enforcement with pwscore, and completed the mandatory single-node restart/recovery evidence protocol.","actions_performed":["Inspected existing libpwquality install and empty pwquality.conf.d/ drop-in directory","Created /etc/security/pwquality.conf.d/10-complexity.conf with minlen=12 and minclass=3","Confirmed pam_pwquality.so is wired into /etc/pam.d/system-auth and /etc/pam.d/password-auth","Created a throwaway test user and used pwscore to confirm a <12-char password fails, a 12+ char 2-class password fails minclass, and a 12+ char 3-class random password passes","Deleted the test user","Captured pre-restart boot_id and re-verified config/PAM state","Issued a backgrounded systemctl reboot on node1 so the ack returned before disconnection","Polled node1 until exec succeeded again, confirming a new boot_id","Re-verified post-reboot: config file present, PAM wiring present, weak password rejected, valid 12-char/3-class password accepted"],"evidence":[{"requirement":"New user passwords require minlen=12 and at least 3 character classes","command_ids":["cmd-b7d4d